    "image_with_text_WnCyE4": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_MrnHMV": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<em>You'll see it the very first time</em>",
            "heading_size": "title-md",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "highlighted_text": "full_text",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle",
            "highlighted_reveal": false
          }
        },
        "text_wRLLtQ": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Clinicians note that the immediate drop in puffiness after drainage is simply <strong>fluid leaving the tissue</strong> — not anything structural. The warmth opens blood flow within the first minute, and the rollers start guiding backed-up fluid down and out.</p><p>The first time you use it, you'll likely feel your neck loosen, a light \"freshness\" as things start moving — and see your face look a little less full, a little more defined, right after.</p><p>That instant hit fades for everyone, with every method, because the fluid comes back. Which is exactly why making the daily version <strong>effortless</strong> is the whole point.</p>",
            "text_font": "body",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_line_height": 1.6,
            "text_letter_spacing": 0,
            "text_capitalize": false,
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
